          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The objects of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} equivariant stable homotopy theory
            – genuine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-spectra"} G-spectra
            – are very rich: Already the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+spectra"} fixed point spectra
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+suspension+spectra"} equivariant suspension spectra
            contain considerably more information than just the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectra"} suspension spectra
            of the plain underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+spaces"} fixed point spaces
            – the latter are just the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+fixed+point+spectra"}> geometric fixed point spectra
              \.
          %p
            The
            %em tom Dieck splitting
            (
            %a{:href => "#tomDieck75"}> tom Dieck 75
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#LewisMaySteinberger86"} Lewis-May-Steinberger 86, V.11
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge summands
            appearing in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+spectra"} fixed point spectra
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+suspension+spectra"} equivariant suspension spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+fixed+point+spectra"} geometric fixed point spectra
            and then have one summand for each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+class"} conjugacy class
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \subset G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectra"} suspension spectra
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+spaces"} fixed point spaces
            by the corresponding
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+group"} Weyl group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
          %p
            Induced from this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
            splitting formula for the spectra themselves is a corresponding
            = succeed "-formula" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+groups"} equivariant stable homotopy groups
            in terms of plain
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
          %p
            The richness of this splitting, hence of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-spectra"} G-spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+groups"} equivariant stable homotopy groups
            of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+sphere+spectrum"} equivariant sphere spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            underlying the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burnside+ring"} Burnside ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} freely generated
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ForTheEquivariantSphereSpectrum"} below
          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\subset G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi H
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [H \subset G]
                for its
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+class"} conjugacy class
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi G
                      %mi H
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi G
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_G H \coloneqq (N_G H)/H
                for its
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+group"} Weyl group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient group
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normalizer+subgroup"} normalizer subgroup
                (of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
                in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi G
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E W_G H
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+bundle"} universal principal bundle
                of the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+group"} Weyl group
          %h3#OfFixedPointSpectraOfEquivariantSuspensionSpectra Of fixed point spectra of equivariant suspension spectra
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+spectrum"} fixed point spectrum
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+suspension+spectrum"} equivariant suspension spectrum
            is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
            formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi G
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi H
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi G
                  %mi H
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mo ∧
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi G
                      %mi H
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F^G(\Sigma^\infty_G X)
                  \\simeq
                  \\underset{[H\subset G]}{\bigvee}
                  \\Sigma^\infty( E (W_G H)_+ \wedge_{W_G H} X^H )
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty
            is the plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
            construction.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GuillouMay12"} Guillou-May 12, theorem 5.3
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Schwede15"} Schwede 15, example 7.7
          %p
            In particular, since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi G
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_G G = 1
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi G
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_G 1 = G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H = G
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H = 1
            are just the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
            of the plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+space"} fixed point space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^G
            and of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\sslash G
            (equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+construction"} Borel construction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \sslash G \simeq E G_+ \times_G X
            ) of the full space, respectively:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi G
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∨
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi H
                            %mo ⊂
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ≠
                            %mi H
                            %mo ≠
                            %mi G
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi G
                    %mi H
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mo ∧
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mi G
                        %mi H
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo ∨
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi G
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F^G(\Sigma^\infty_G X)
                  \\simeq
                  \\Sigma^\infty( X^G )
                  \\vee
                  \\left(
                  \\underset{{[H\subset G]} \atop {1 \neq H \neq G}}{\bigvee}
                  \\Sigma^\infty( E (W_G H)_+ \wedge_{W_G H} X^H )
                  \\right)
                  \\vee
                  \\Sigma^\infty( E G_+ \wedge_{G} X )
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here the first summand is the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+fixed+point+spectrum"} geometric fixed point spectrum
            inside the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+spectrum"} fixed point spectrum
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Φ
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi G
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi G
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Phi^G(\Sigma^\infty_G X)
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\Sigma^\infty( X^G )
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  F^G(\Sigma^\infty_G X)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Schwede15"}> Schwede 15, Example 7.7
            )
          %h3#for_equivariant_homotopy_groups For equivariant homotopy groups
          %p
            It follows that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a pointed
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-space"} topological G-space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+groups"} equivariant homotopy groups
            are
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi π
                            %mo •
                            %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mn ∞
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi H
                              %mo ⊂
                              %mi G
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %msubsup
                            %mi π
                            %mo •
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi W
                                %mi G
                              %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi W
                            %mi G
                          %mi H
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                          %mo ∧
                          %msup
                            %mi X
                            %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mn ∞
                          %msup
                            %mi X
                            %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊕
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                            %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                  %mi H
                                  %mo ⊂
                                  %mi G
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mrow
                                %mrow
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mo ≠
                                  %mi H
                                  %mo ≠
                                  %mi G
                          %msubsup
                            %mi π
                            %mo •
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi W
                                %mi G
                              %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi W
                            %mi G
                          %mi H
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                          %mo ∧
                          %msup
                            %mi X
                            %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊕
                          %msubsup
                            %mi π
                            %mo •
                            %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mo +
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\pi_\bullet^G(\Sigma^\infty X)
                  \&amp;
                  \\simeq
                  \\underset{[H \subset G]}{\bigoplus}
                  \\pi_\bullet^{W_G H}(\Sigma^\infty (E (W_G H)_+ \wedge X^H))
                  \\\
                  \&amp;\simeq
                  \\pi_\bullet(\Sigma^\infty X^G)
                  \\oplus
                  \\underset{{[H \subset G]} \atop {1 \neq H \neq G}}{\bigoplus}
                  \\pi_\bullet^{W_G H}(\Sigma^\infty (E (W_G H)_+ \wedge X^H))
                  \\oplus
                  \\pi_\bullet^{G}(\Sigma^\infty (E G_+ \wedge X))
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            is over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Schwede15"} Schwede 15, theorem 6.12
          %h3#for_rational_equivariant_homotopy_theory For rational equivariant homotopy theory
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            finite and for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} rational equivariant stable homotopy theory
            this becomes (
            %a{:href => "#Greenlees"}> Greenlees, 6.2
            )
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi RationalSpectra
                  %mo ≃
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi H
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi G
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G RationalSpectra \simeq \underset{[H \subset G] }{\prod} \mathbb{Q}(W_G H) Mod
          %p
            where the product is over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi G
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_G H
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+group"} Weyl group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#ForTheEquivariantSphereSpectrum For the equivariant sphere spectrum
          %p
            For the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+sphere+spectrum"} equivariant sphere spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi G
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S} = \Sigma^\infty_G S^0
            the tom Dieck splitting says that its 0th
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+group"} equivariant homotopy group
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
            on the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %munder
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi H
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msubsup
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo +
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi E
                  %mi W
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                  %mtext conjugacy classes of subgroups
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_0^G(\mathbb{S})
                  \\simeq
                  \\underset{[H \subset G]}{\oplus} \pi_0^{W H}(\Sigma_+^\infty E W H)
                  \\simeq
                  \\mathbb{Z}\big[\text{conjugacy classes of subgroups}\big]
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Schwede15"} Schwede 15, p. 64
          %p
            This is the group underlying the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burnside+ring"} Burnside ring
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Whitehead+theorem"} equivariant Whitehead theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elmendorf%27s+theorem"} Elmendorf's theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-CW+approximation"} G-CW approximation
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The theorem at the level of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#tomDieck75
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tammo+tom+Dieck"}> Tammo tom Dieck
              , Satz 2 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Orbittypen und äquivariante Homologie. II.
          %p
            The refinement to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            is achieved in section V.11 of
          %ul
            %li#LewisMaySteinberger86
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L.+Gaunce+Lewis"}> L. Gaunce Lewis
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant stable homotopy theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/equi.pdf"} pdf
          %p An alternative proof is in
          %ul
            %li#GuillouMay12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bert+Guillou"}> Bert Guillou
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Permutative
                  = succeed "-categories" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1207.3459"} arXiv:1207.3459
          %p Detailed lecture notes are in
          %ul
            %li#Schwede15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
                , section 6 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lectures+on+Equivariant+Stable+Homotopy+Theory"} Lectures on Equivariant Stable Homotopy Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/people/schwede/equivariant.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Blumberg17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"}> Andrew Blumberg
                , section 2.7 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Burnside category
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/a.debray/lecture_notes/m392c_EHT_notes.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://github.com/adebray/equivariant_homotopy_theory"} GitHub
          %p
            A brief mentioning appears in this survey of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} rational equivariant stable homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li#Greenlees
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Greenlees"}> John Greenlees
              , p. 3 of
              %em Triangulated categories of rational equivariant cohomology theories
              (
              %a{:href => "https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/eda8/ee6effb2ae487085a2e7615a4a7e1964c493.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GreenleesRationalEquivariant.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
